. It would apply to renters and landlords, and lease terms that try to waive these rules would be void. The change would take effect the day after final passage and apply to leases signed on or after that date.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MN-2025-SF390":{"id":"MN-2025-SF390","passed":false,"number":"SF 390","title":"Safe routes to school grant program bond issue and appropriation","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2025-01-21","sponsor":{"name":"Pappas","party":"Democratic-Farmer-Labor","state":"MN","district":"65"},"cosponsors":[{"name":"Housley","party":"R","state":"MN","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Rasmusson","party":"R","state":"MN","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Johnson Stewart","party":"Democratic-Farmer-Labor","state":"MN","date":null,"withdrawn":false}],"cosponsorCount":3,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-05-17","text":"Authors added Rasmusson; Johnson Stewart","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-05-15","text":"Comm report: To pass","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-05-15","text":"Second reading","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2025-05-09","text":"Comm report: To pass and re-referred to Finance","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2025-01-21","text":"Introduction and first reading","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2025-01-21","text":"Referred to Capital Investment","chamber":"Senate"}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Bonds, Transportation and Transportation Department","url":"https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2025/0/SF/390?body=Senate","textUrl":"https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2025/0/SF/390/versions/0/","versions":[{"label":"Introduction","date":"2025-01-16","url":"https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2025/0/SF/390/versions/0/","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would set aside $10 million for grants in the safe routes to school program, which helps pay for safer ways for students to get to school. It would also let the state sell up to $10 million in bonds, which are borrowed money the state must pay back. The money would go to the transportation commissioner, and the section would take effect the day after final passage.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MN-2025-HF5159":{"id":"MN-2025-HF5159","passed":false,"number":"HF 5159","title":"Nonferrous mining prohibited if sulfate levels increase in waters within the Rainy River headwaters, and penalties established.","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-05-17","sponsor":{"name":"Falconer","party":"Democratic-Farmer-Labor","state":"MN","district":"49A"},"cosponsors":[{"name":"Kraft","party":"Democratic-Farmer-Labor","state":"MN","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Kozlowski","party":"Democratic-Farmer-Labor","state":"MN","date":null,"withdrawn":false}],"cosponsorCount":2,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-05-17","text":"Introduction and first reading, referred to Environment and Natural Resources Finance and Policy","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-05-17","text":"Authors added Kraft and Kozlowski","chamber":"House"}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Mines and Mining, Natural Resources Department, Water, Water Resources, and Waterways","url":"https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2026/0/HF/5159?body=House","textUrl":"https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2026/0/HF/5159/versions/0/","versions":[{"label":"Introduction","date":"2026-05-16","url":"https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2026/0/HF/5159/versions/0/","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would bar permits for nonferrous metallic mining in the Rainy River headwaters unless the mine is not expected to raise sulfate levels in water by more than zero parts per million, and it would require water monitoring to be posted online. If a mine causes a sulfate increase above that level, the commissioner of natural 