ng, referred to Health Finance and Policy","chamber":"House"}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Data Practices and Privacy, Health and Health Department, Marriage and Marriage Dissolution","url":"https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2026/0/HF/5152?body=House","textUrl":"https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2026/0/HF/5152/versions/0/","versions":[{"label":"Introduction","date":"2026-05-14","url":"https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2026/0/HF/5152/versions/0/","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would let a person ask to change or add a sex indicator on a birth record, and it would let certain people request the same kind of change on a death record. It would also let some marriage records be modified and would make older replaced records private data that can be shared only by court order. The commissioner would have to offer at least three sex marker choices, including an \"X.\"","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MN-2025-HF4102":{"id":"MN-2025-HF4102","passed":false,"number":"HF 4102","title":"State Patrol compensation study requirements modified, and volunteer chaplains allowed within the state patrol.","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-09","sponsor":{"name":"Koznick","party":"R","state":"MN","district":"57A"},"cosponsors":[{"name":"Hoffman","party":"Democratic-Farmer-Labor","state":"MN","date":null,"withdrawn":false}],"cosponsorCount":1,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-05-17","text":"Motion did not prevail for urgency, rules suspension, pursuant to rule 34.1","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-05-12","text":"Comm report: Rule 45-amend, subst. General Orders SF4273","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-05-12","text":"Second reading","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-05-11","text":"Received from House","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-05-11","text":"Introduction and first reading","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"202